.TH GRABIT 1 "2026-07-05" "grabit 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grabit \- screenshot, screen-recording, OCR, and uploader for wlroots Wayland compositors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grabit
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B grabit
.BR set | get | unset
.RI [ key "] [" value ]
.br
.B grabit
.B sxcu
.RB { add | list | show | remove }
.RI [ arg ]
.br
.B grabit
.B plugin
.RB { install | list | show | update | remove }
.RI [ arg ]
.br
.B grabit
.B help
.RI [ subcommand ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B grabit
captures region screenshots, records the screen, performs OCR, and uploads the
result, with a native freeze + region selector (no
.BR slurp / grim
shellouts). It uses
.B zwlr_screencopy_v1
when advertised, otherwise falls back to
.B ext_image_copy_capture_v1
(KDE Plasma 6).
.PP
Supported compositors: Hyprland, sway, niri, river, KDE Plasma 6. X11 and GNOME
are not supported.
.PP
With no action flag, grabit performs the configured
.B default_action
(seeded to
.B copy
on first run, which also writes a default config to
.IR ~/.config/grabit/config.toml ).
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-copy
Copy the screenshot to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload
Upload the screenshot to the default service (the
.B service
config key).
.TP
.BI \-\- service
Upload to a specific built-in service
.RB ( zipline ,
.BR nest ,
.BR fakecrime ,
.BR ez ,
.BR guns ,
.BR pixelvault )
or a registered
.B .sxcu
uploader.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output ", " \-\-save
Capture, save to disk, and print the path to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-record
Toggle screen recording (run again to stop). Records a region to MP4/H.264
(or WebM/GIF via
.BR "grabit set recording.format webm|gif" )
with a live border overlay and an SNI tray icon.
.TP
.B \-\-pin
Capture a region and pin it to the desktop as a click-through overlay. Pins
stack and persist as long-lived processes.
.TP
.BR \-\-grab ", " \-\-release ", " \-\-close\-all
Make existing pins interactive (clickable close button + draggable), restore
them to click-through, or dismiss every pin. Intended to be wired to a
compositor hold-bind.
.TP
.B \-\-tesseract
Capture a region, OCR it via
.BR tesseract ,
and copy the text to the clipboard. Requires
.B tesseract
on
.B $PATH
plus
.IR eng.traineddata .
.TP
.BI \-\-translate [=lang]
With
.BR \-\-tesseract :
pipe the OCR text through translate-shell's
.B trans
binary and copy the translation instead.
.I lang
is the target language (default
.BR en ;
source auto-detected). Falls back to raw OCR if
.B trans
is missing or the call fails (20s cap).
.TP
.B \-\-show
With
.BR \-\-tesseract :
render the OCR/translate result on screen as a transient click-through text card
instead of copying. Auto-dismisses after
.B text_card.dismiss_secs
(default 8s).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-edit
Open the in-tree annotation editor before the action (pen, marker, line,
rect, ellipse, arrow, blur, text, eraser, HSL color picker + eyedropper).
Pairs with any action. Make it the default with
.BR "grabit set edit.default true" .
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fullscreen
Capture a whole monitor instead of dragging a region. With one monitor it is
grabbed directly. With several, the selector opens dimmed and snaps to whole
monitors \(em hover a monitor to highlight it and click to grab it (dragging
still works for a custom region). Pairs with any capture action, including
.BR \-\-record ,
and with
.BR \-e ;
cannot be combined with
.BR \-f .
.TP
.BI \-\-fullscreen= monitor
As above, but capture a specific monitor directly (no picker).
.I monitor
is a 1-based number or an output name (e.g.
.BR \-\-fullscreen=DP\-1 ).
Use
.B \-\-fullscreen=all
to capture every monitor stitched into one image. An unknown value lists the
available monitors and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-cursor
Include the mouse pointer in the screenshot for this run even if
.B capture.cursor
is
.BR false .
The pointer is included by default; hide it with
.BR "grabit set capture.cursor false" .
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Upload to Zipline in chunks via its partial-upload API (useful behind
Cloudflare's upload size limit). Make it permanent with
.B "grabit set services.zipline.chunked true"
and tune the chunk size (MiB) with
.BR services.zipline.chunk_size .
Plain uploads rejected with HTTP 413 (e.g. Cloudflare's 100MB cap) retry in
chunks automatically, halving the chunk size if needed. Zipline only; other
services ignore it.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Use an existing
.I file
instead of capturing.
.TP
.BI \-\-filename " tpl"
Per-run filename template (overrides the
.B filename
config key). See
.BR "FILENAME TEMPLATES" .
.TP
.BI \-\-format " fmt"
Per-run output format:
.BR png ,
.BR jpeg ,
or
.B webp
(default
.BR png ).
JPEG/WebP must have been compiled in.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-upload
With
.BR \-\-record :
skip the auto-upload after recording even if
.BR default_action=upload .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tray
Suppress the SNI tray icon during recording.
.TP
.BR \-\-silent ", " \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress notifications and sound (errors still print).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug logging to standard error (same as
.BR GRABIT_DEBUG=1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; the following argument is treated as
.BI \-f " file" .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config
Open the on-screen settings window: a floating toplevel with the keys grouped
into tabs (general, recording, editor, image, ocr, notify). Each key gets a
widget for its type \(em a toggle for bools,
.RB \(lq< value >\(rq
steppers for enums and numbers, an editable text field for strings, a
.RB \(lq ... \(rq
file/folder picker for path keys (needs
.B zenity
or
.BR kdialog ),
and a dropdown of connected monitors for the monitor keys. Arrow keys (or
.BR hjkl )
move and change,
.B Tab
switches tab,
.B Enter
edits or opens the focused row, and the mouse works throughout. Changes apply
live \(em every edit is written immediately and the previous config is backed
up to
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit-config.bak.toml
so it can be restored.
.B Esc
closes.
.TP
.BI "set " "key value"
Write a config key (schema-validated).
.TP
.BI "set " key
Print the example/default value for that key.
.TP
.B set
List all settable keys.
.TP
.BI "get " [key]
Print one config key, or dump every set key.
.TP
.BI "unset " key
Remove a config key.
.TP
.BI "help " [subcommand]
Print help for a subcommand
.RB ( set ,
.BR get ,
.BR unset ,
.BR sxcu ,
.BR plugin ).
.SS Custom uploaders (ShareX .sxcu)
.TP
.BI "sxcu add " file
Parse, sanitize, and register a
.B .sxcu
uploader; use it as
.BI \-\- name .
.TP
.B sxcu list
Show registered uploaders (alias:
.BR ls ).
.TP
.BI "sxcu show " name
Print parsed fields.
.TP
.BI "sxcu remove " name
Remove an uploader (alias:
.BR rm ).
.SS Plugins
.TP
.BI "plugin install " git\-url
Clone, build, and install a plugin.
.TP
.B plugin list
List installed plugins.
.TP
.BI "plugin show " name
Print the parsed manifest.
.TP
.BI "plugin update " [name]
Update one plugin, or all of them.
.TP
.BI "plugin remove " name
Uninstall a plugin.
.TP
.BI name " ..."
Run the installed plugin
.BI grabit\- name
(auto-updates in the background per its manifest). With
.BI \-p " name"
the plugin's last stdout line is pinned to the desktop as a file.
Plugins with
.B capture.auto
receive a fresh screenshot path as their first argument;
.B \-\-capture
and
.B \-\-no\-capture
override that per call. See
.B PLUGINS.md
for the manifest format.
.SH FILENAME TEMPLATES
Tokens accepted by
.B \-\-filename
and the
.B filename
config key:
.TP
.B %Y %m %d %H %M %S
strftime date/time fields.
.TP
.B %s
Unix timestamp.
.TP
.BR %r [ N ]
Random alphanumeric,
.I N
characters (default 12).
.TP
.B %u
UUID v4.
.TP
.B %w
Active window class (Hyprland IPC; empty elsewhere).
.TP
.B %t
Active window title (Hyprland IPC; empty elsewhere).
.TP
.B %o
Output name where the capture happened.
.TP
.B %%
Literal
.BR % .
.PP
Presets via the
.B filename_preset
key:
.B date
.RB ( %Y\-%m\-%d\-%H\-%M\-%S ,
default),
.B random
.RB ( %r12 ),
.B uuid
.RB ( %u ),
.B timestamp
.RB ( %s ).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config lives at
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/grabit/config.toml
(else
.IR ~/.config/grabit/config.toml ),
written with mode 0600. Manage it with
.B grabit set/get/unset
or edit the TOML directly. Notable top-level keys:
.B default_action
.RB ( copy / upload / save / pin ),
.BR service ,
.BR notifications ,
.BR also_save ,
.BR save_dir ,
.BR editor ,
.BR filename ,
.BR filename_preset ,
.BR format .
Per-service auth tokens go under
.BI services. name .auth
or, preferred, the
.BI GRABIT_ SERVICE _AUTH
environment variable.
To keep the token out of the config file, set
.BI services. name .auth_cmd
to a shell command that prints it, e.g.
.BR "grabit set services.zipline.auth_cmd \(dqpass show grabit/zipline\(dq" .
It is run through
.BR "/bin/sh -c" ,
and its first output line (trimmed) is used as the token.
Resolution order is the environment variable, then
.BR auth_cmd ,
then the plaintext
.BR auth .
.PP
Set
.B region.confirm
to
.B true
to keep the selection adjustable after releasing the drag (flameshot-style):
resize it with the handles or
.BR Shift+arrows ,
move it by dragging inside it or with the
.B arrow keys
(hold to accelerate),
drag outside it to start over, then press
.BR Enter ,
press
.BR Ctrl+C ,
or double-click inside it to capture;
.B Esc
cancels. In any selector,
.B Ctrl+A
selects the whole monitor under the cursor.
.PP
See
.B OPTIONS.md
for the full key reference (capture backend, region snap/confirm, encoder
quality, recording, sound, pin, OCR/translate, preview/text card, edit
defaults).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GRABIT_DEBUG
If set to
.BR 1 ,
enable debug logging (same as
.BR \-d ).
.TP
.BI GRABIT_ SERVICE _AUTH
Per-service auth token, overriding config.
.I SERVICE
is one of
.BR ZIPLINE ,
.BR NEST ,
.BR FAKECRIME ,
.BR EZ ,
.BR GUNS ,
.BR PIXELVAULT .
.TP
.B GRABIT_BIN
Set by plugin dispatch; absolute path to the grabit binary.
.TP
.BR GRABIT_PLUGIN_NAME ", " GRABIT_PLUGIN_DIR ", " GRABIT_CACHE_DIR
Also set by plugin dispatch: the plugin's name, install directory, and
per-plugin cache directory. See
.BR PLUGINS.md .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Holds the recording pid file and per-pin IPC sockets (falls back to
.IR /tmp ).
.TP
.B XDG_VIDEOS_DIR
Recording save directory. The
.B save_dir
config key takes precedence; otherwise this variable is used, falling back to
.IR ~/Videos .
Screenshots use
.B save_dir
else
.IR ~/Pictures .
.TP
.B TESSDATA_PREFIX
Tesseract language-data directory.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color in logs (https://no-color.org).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/grabit/config.toml
User configuration (TOML).
.TP
.I ~/.config/grabit/uploaders/<name>.sxcu
Registered ShareX uploaders.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit-show.pid
PID file for the on-screen text/preview card.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit-config.bak.toml
Backup of the configuration taken when
.B config
opens, for reverting live edits.
.TP
.I ~/.config/grabit/plugins/<name>/
Installed plugins (binaries symlinked from
.IR plugins/.bin/ ;
per-plugin cache under
.IR ~/.cache/grabit/plugins/<name>/ ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B grabit \-c
Region screenshot to the clipboard.
.TP
.B grabit \-u
Upload using the
.B service
config key.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-zipline
Upload to a specific service.
.TP
.B grabit \-o > shot.txt
Save and capture the path.
.TP
.B grabit \-F \-o
Save a whole-monitor screenshot.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-fullscreen=DP\-1 \-c
Copy monitor DP-1 to the clipboard.
.TP
.B grabit \-e \-u
Annotate, then upload.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-record
Start recording (re-run to stop).
.TP
.B grabit \-\-pin
Pin a region to the desktop.
.TP
.B grabit \-f shot.png \-\-zipline
Upload an existing file.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-tesseract \-\-translate=ja
OCR a region and copy the Japanese translation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and non-zero on error.
